{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789915785,"nonce":"uJa9afVOsnrKxUEYt6P3F0vvwgc=","title":"`this.method()` inside an abstract over a built-in resolved to the abstract's own method","message":"`abstract A(Array\u003cInt\u003e) { public function toString() return this.toString(); }`\nrecursed until the stack overflowed (silent exit): `resolve_method_symbol`'s\n`This` arm ignored `this_type` and looked the name up in the current\nclass's methods. `haxe.Rest.toString` is the stdlib instance.\n\nFix, narrow: when the current class is an abstract and `this_type` resolves\nto no class symbol (Array, String, a typedef of one), skip the current-class\nlookup and fall through to the receiver-type resolution. Over a class or\ninterface the abstract's own methods still answer first: `haxe.ds.Map`'s\n`this.set(k, v)` is bound to `Map.set` and rerouted to the runtime maps by\nname, and resolving it on `IMap` left `copy` unresolvable.","files":null}]}